<%# The words under the artwork, whoever speaks them, plus the credit line —
    extracted (story 0032) so the front door's sit gate and the ungated
    archive/preview render the SAME text from one place. Locals: pick,
    painting.

    The curator's note is shown whole — rule 8, amended by 0032: whole once
    revealed; only its entrance is gated, and only on `/`. Museum copy keeps
    the archive's clamp + More treatment; inside the gate the expand
    controller re-measures on the details toggle (it reads 0×0 in a closed
    details — see expand_controller.js). %>
<% if pick.hand_written? %>
  <div class="label__note" id="daily-note"><%= simple_format(pick.note) %></div>
<% elsif pick.note.present? %>
  <div class="label__body" id="daily-note" data-controller="expand">
    <p class="label__text" data-expand-target="text"><%= pick.note %></p>
    <button type="button" class="label__more" data-expand-target="button"
            data-action="expand#toggle" hidden>More</button>
    <p class="label__source">From <%= painting.source_name %></p>
  </div>
<% end %>
<%# Neither voice has words (owner direction, 2026-08-31): render NOTHING —
    an empty shell with a dangling "From <museum>" line read as a broken
    promise. Auto-filled days can't reach this (0023 requires a description);
    a hand-picked day can, and it degrades to picture + credit, quietly. %>

<%= tag.p(painting.credit_line, class: "label__credit") if painting.credit_line.present? %>
